Sound wasn't working. Google ai said a recent linux update
could cause the "dummy output" problem. This was how to correct it.

Something about using the old blah blah. 

It seems to be okay this way but i don't know if it's really useful
or necessary.

@code sh
rachel@redsandsofmars:~/notes (main)
$ echo "options snd-hda-intel dmic_detect=0" | sudo tee /etc/modprobe.d/alsa-base.conf


rachel@redsandsofmars:~/notes (main)
$ cat /etc/modprobe.d/alsa-base.conf
options snd-hda-intel dmic_detect=0
@end
